x;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135001203.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Union shipping minister Sarbananda Sonowal confirmed that two vessels carrying Indian seafarers were attacked in October. The MT ST 3 was struck by a projectile in the Strait of Hormuz, while the YARA J was hit by a drone off Romania. Fortunately, all 24 Indian nationals aboard both vessels are reported safe and unharmed. India has condemned attacks on commercial vessels, citing concerns for the safety of seafarers.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/two-vessels-carrying-24-indian-seafarers-hit-by-projectiles-drone-in-separate-incidents-all-safe/articleshow/135001203.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/two-vessels-carrying-24-indian-seafarers-hit-by-projectiles-drone-in-separate-incidents-all-safe/articleshow/135001203.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-16T23:29:10+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Yashasvi Vasistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135001298,imgsize-41564.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[NCW steps in after video shows senior J&amp;K IAS officer 'abusing' woman subordinate]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/ncw-steps-in-after-video-shows-senior-jk-ias-officer-abusing-woman-subordinate/articleshow/134997738.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134997738.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/ncw-steps-in-after-video-shows-senior-jk-ias-officer-abusing-woman-subordinate/articleshow/134997738.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/ncw-steps-in-after-video-shows-senior-jk-ias-officer-abusing-woman-subordinate/articleshow/134997738.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-16T20:35:50+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Karan Manral</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134998120,imgsize-652646.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[India diversified crude oil sources from 27 to 41 amid disruptions in Hormuz, Red Sea: Hardeep Puri]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/india-diversified-crude-oil-sources-from-27-to-41-amid-disruptions-in-hormuz-red-sea-hardeep-puri/articleshow/134997542.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134997542.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[India has expanded its crude oil supply sources from 27 to 41 countries to improve energy security. The government is also increasing its refining capacity and exploring new oil sources in response to geopolitical concerns. Minister Hardeep Singh Puri emphasized the impact of global shipping disruptions on domestic industries and households. He outlined plans to enhance domestic energy production through initiatives like the Samudra Manthan scheme.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/india-diversified-crude-oil-sources-from-27-to-41-amid-disruptions-in-hormuz-red-sea-hardeep-puri/articleshow/134997542.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/india-diversified-crude-oil-sources-from-27-to-41-amid-disruptions-in-hormuz-red-sea-hardeep-puri/articleshow/134997542.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-16T19:59:15+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Pranjal Pandey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134997566,imgsize-66224.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['While with Nitish, I got 9 people murdered': Anant Singh's shocking claim, then clarification]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/while-with-nitish-i-got-9-people-murdered-anant-singhs-shocking-claim-then-clarification/articleshow/134997378.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134997378.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Recalling his sacrifices for Nitish Kumar, Anant Snigh claimed: “Who has made as many sacrifices as I have? Nitish Kumar was nothing back then. He used to roam around here and there. At that time, while being with Nitish Kumar, I got nine people murdered,” Singh said. However, later the leader clarified that his remarks was misinterpreted and that he was referring to the killing of nine of his associates.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/while-with-nitish-i-got-9-people-murdered-anant-singhs-shocking-claim-then-clarification/articleshow/134997378.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/while-with-nitish-i-got-9-people-murdered-anant-singhs-shocking-claim-then-clarification/articleshow/134997378.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-16T19:58:56+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rajeev Singh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134997564,imgsize-58340.cms"/></item></channel></rss>